# Vite 8 and jsdom 30 need Node 22.19+, and the testing toolchain
# (why-is-node-running 3.x) narrows that to ^22.22.2 || ^24.15.0 || >=26.
# The three package.json files declare the floor, which is the load-bearing
# part: npm warns on a mismatch, and Vercel reads it to pick a runtime.
#
# engine-strict is deliberately left OFF. It turns that warning into a hard
# install failure, and `npm install` also runs inside Vercel's build, so
# enabling it would make a deploy break on a runtime version we do not control
# from here. Enable it per-machine, or on CI, once the pinned Node is
# guaranteed:
#
#   engine-strict=true
